[{"id":"VRCE-6-32-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":32,"verse":1,"english":"Then those Rākşasas, going to that subduer of enemies, Rāvana, informed him that Rāma along with the monkeys had laid siege to the city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-42-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6032001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d7eac414697227662fbc2f932de30c52db3bca3979d0112f94c7c577aa8dd58","compact":"db6128bc5ff26b5862e27faa79964dd663ba86dc0be74bfe07fe75cedac0162a","nasal":"963ddb92e5d6678c60d22d6dca2b811f652e6902697a03db37b6f2278322d055"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-32-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":32,"verse":2,"english":"Hearing the city besieged, the night-ranger was enraged. And, hearing that double arrangements had been made (by Rāma) in guarding the gateways (Råvaņa) ascended the palace.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.757,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-42-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6032002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d45d1f9c99847b675c299696375a11d7db6d109a3dd4898a2fd605dfdb44ff69","compact":"3aca7324af436361e0a14f9ae32ac91d851ab6a972aacc87d66c4f8f09afe857","nasal":"3aca7324af436361e0a14f9ae32ac91d851ab6a972aacc87d66c4f8f09afe857"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-32-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":32,"verse":3,"english":"He saw Lanka with her hills, woods, and forests, covered everywhere with innumerable monkeys eager for encounter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.641,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-42-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6032003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74fe7a453131b4dce8453e1bdbfddf2218ee803c767c8a09c97546aad82349df","compact":"94b4aa95bd8c358